<title>USA: Flores completes sale of US Gulf field interest.</title>
<headline>Flores completes sale of US Gulf field interest.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flores &amp; Rucks Inc said Thursday that it had completed the sale of its interest in the South Marsh Island 269 field to Norcen Energy Resources.</p>
<p>Flores said in a release that it realized proceeds of $37.2 million from the sale of its non-operating interest of about 20 percent in three blocks in the field.</p>
<p>FNR is a U.S. independent oil and gas exploration and development company with assets concentrated in oil interests in the Mississippi Delta region.</p>
<p>((-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623))</p>
</text>
